    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 0 failures/errors).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe task required all rejection responses (400, 409, 429) to return an RFC7807 `application/problem+json` body with `type`, `title`, `status` and `detail`, while keeping the HTTP status codes unchanged.\n\n**Architecture finding:** Rejections in this app are produced exclusively by escalation handlers under `rest/escalation/`. OfficeFloor's `SpringHttpObjectResponderFactory` delegates response rendering to Spring MVC's return-value handlers, so returning a `ResponseEntity<ProblemDetail>` automatically yields `application/problem+json` \u2014 which is why the already-compliant `ValidationExceptionHandler` and `GeneralExceptionHandler` worked. A reusable `ProblemDetails.build(ex, status, detail)` helper already existed, populating `type` (`about:blank`), `title`, `status` and `detail`.\n\n**Changes** \u2014 converted the eight non-compliant handlers from plain `Map`/empty `Void` bodies to `ResponseEntity<ProblemDetail>` via `ProblemDetails.build`:\n\n- **400:** `MissingOwnerFields`, `InvalidEmail`, `InvalidPostcode`, `InvalidTelephone`, `FutureRegistrationDate` \u2014 now problem+json; each retains its field-level info as an `errors` extension member.\n- **409:** `CityAtCapacity`, `DuplicateIdentity` \u2014 previously empty bodies, now problem+json.\n- **429:** `DailyOwnerLimit` \u2014 previously empty body, now problem+json.\n\nStatus codes are unchanged (`BAD_REQUEST`/`CONFLICT`/`TOO_MANY_REQUESTS`). The new `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectionIsProblemJson` and the full suite pass.\n\nOne deliberate behavior change worth flagging: the 400 handlers previously returned a bare `{\"errors\":[...]}` JSON shape; that top-level shape is now RFC7807, with the field list moved under the `errors` extension member. No existing test depended on the old shape, but any external client parsing `$.errors` at the root would need updating.",
